<h2 class="g-h2" id="what-this-is">What this is</h2>
<div class="g-prose">
  <p>The citator preview is a static site: Eleventy renders Nunjucks templates, Tailwind builds the stylesheet from CourtListener's design tokens, and Alpine's CSP build runs the interactive parts. This guide documents that interface one part at a time. Each page shows the part working, the snippet that renders it, its parameters and data, the script it needs, and the files to copy.</p>
  <p>Nothing here is a reimplementation. The macros, partials, styles and scripts are the app's, copied in by <code>npm run sync</code>, so what you see is what the app ships. The full pages at the end of the sidebar are the app's real pages, built from the same fixtures.</p>
</div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="how-to-read-a-page">How to read a page</h2>
<div class="g-prose">
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Example</strong>: the part rendered live. Every example sits on its own; <em>Copy page</em> exports a complete app page with setup and scripts. Reader-dependent parts export the actual reader host; visual states and illustrative data are labelled.</li>
    <li><strong>Parameters</strong>: the macro's arguments, or the data a partial reads, with their types and defaults.</li>
    <li><strong>Behaviour</strong>: the script that drives the part, the markup it expects, and the keyboard and focus rules it keeps.</li>
    <li><strong>Files</strong>: what to bring into another project for the part to work.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Pages read in order: the link at the foot of each page goes to the next. <kbd>⌘K</kbd> finds a page; <kbd>⌘\</kbd> folds the sidebar away.</p>
</div>

